/*  The view: what the field looks like.

    It takes squares and gives back lines. It does not print them and it does not know what a key
    means — the main program prints, and the controller decides what moves. A view that printed
    would be a view you could not check by comparing its answer to an expected one.

    ★ It PULLS the model, so `spot` is in scope here by its short name — including in the
    SIGNATURE below, which is the whole reason this file can exist. A declaration inside a pull
    could not name a pulled type until 2026-09-20: the hoist gathers every signature before any
    pull scope exists, so `given (the series of spot body)` was refused while a body two lines
    down could use `spot` freely. Writing this file is what found it.

    ★ Written inside the pull, this book KEEPS that dependency rather than charging its caller: a
    program that wants a picture asks `screen` and never mentions `board`.

    ⚠ It returns a series of lines rather than one block of text. Joining them is one line at the
    call site and splitting a block back apart is not, so the caller keeps the choice of how to
    space, indent or frame them.
*/

Pull a book on board.
    Define object screen with () and book:

        /// The field as one line of text per row, with an `O` wherever the body lies.
        Bind series of text to frame-of, given (the series of spot body):
            Define picture as a series of text.

            For each row in range 1 to cast board's height, repeat:
                Define line as "".

                For each column in range 1 to cast board's width, repeat:
                    Define here as cast board's at on (row, column).
                    Define filled as false.

                    For each piece in body, repeat:
                        If cast piece's same-as on (here), the filled becomes true.
                    Done.

                    If filled, the line becomes line joined to "O".
                    Otherwise, the line becomes line joined to ".".
                Done.

                Insert line into picture.
            Done.

            Return picture.
        Done.
    Done.
Done.
